KNOWNBUG
default_disable2.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.0\.p0\] always main\.rst == 0: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A 'default disable iff (expr)' (1800-2017 16.15) applies to all concurrent
assertions in the module, including procedural concurrent assertions inside
an always block (16.14.6). Here 'default disable iff (rst);' should disable
'p0: assert property (rst == 0);' whenever rst holds, so p0 must be PROVED.
ebmc instead REFUTES it: the default disable condition is not applied to
procedural concurrent assertions. Root cause in src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp:
verilog_rtl_buildert::build_property wraps module-level assert/assume/cover
conditions in sva_disable_iff_exprt using default_disable_iff, but
verilog_rtl_buildert::build_check (which records assert/assume/cover
statements inside always/initial blocks) never consults default_disable_iff.
A fix must apply the default disable only to concurrent assertions
(ID_verilog_assert_property/assume_property/cover_property), not to immediate
assertions (ID_verilog_immediate_*), which are unaffected by default disable
iff.
